# logs/ and .codex/ (run history + db-history.sqlite index) are deliberately tracked, not
# ignored -- cross-machine visibility into prior SQL runs/failures outweighs repo bloat while
# this project is in active development. Matches road-cal; road-kit ignored .codex/ until
# 2026-08-26, which silently kept its run history local-only.

# Rendered by bin/render-auth-config.sh - carries environment-specific values (a JWKS URL, or an
# Auth0 tenant's issuer/audience under AUTH_PROFILE=external_oidc), so per-machine/per-env, not
# source. 90_rest_auth.generated.sql is the same idea, one file: whether the scaffold's public
# login endpoint deploys at all (spec-patch-09 section 2).
deploy/create/80_standalone.generated.sql
deploy/create/90_rest_auth.generated.sql
